(ned -- GO TO THE C REFERENCE POSE, operator spec 2026-08-03.)
(#4 = side: -1 puts the head at A zero -45 with the taught +dy, +1 mirrors)
(both. These are exactly the two poses cal_c_zero probes from, so what the)
(operator eyeballs is what the measurement will use -- "user just needs to)
(verify and if its in the right ballpark, we are good".)

(The reference is stored as OFFSETS FROM THE PUCK CENTRE -- #3061 in X,)
(#3058 in Y, #3060 below the top -- so it tracks the puck as calibration)
(moves it. Nothing here is absolute: cx, cy and top come from the newest)
(cal_probe_center and the taught numbers hang off them.)

o<cal_c_goto> sub
  #<cx>   = #1
  #<cy>   = #2
  #<top>  = #3
  #<side> = #4

  #<lift> = 25.4
  #<f_tr> = 2500.0
  #<f_ck> = 1000.0
  #<f_ro> = 1200.0

  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, GO TO C REF: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  o6 if [#<top> EQ 0 AND #<cx> EQ 0 AND #<cy> EQ 0]
    (abort, GO TO C REF: no puck centre - run StartPuck first)
  o6 endif
  o7 if [#3058 EQ 0]
    (abort, GO TO C REF: no C reference taught. Press SET C REF, jog the tip into place, then press StartC.)
  o7 endif

  #<zref>  = [#<top> - #3060]
  #<zhigh> = [#<zref> + #<lift>]

  M64 P3
  G4 P1.5

  (rise ONLY if low, then travel and rotate together with Z held -- the same)
  (order cc_probe uses, so the button and the probe cannot disagree)
  (X FIRST, then Y and rotation, then Z -- identical order to cc_probe so the)
  (button and the probe can never disagree about how they approach.)
  G90
  G1 X[#<cx> + #3061] Y[#<cy> + #<side> * #3058] F[#<f_tr>]
  G1 A[#3069 + #<side> * 45] C#3070 F[#<f_ro>]
  o20 if [#5422 LT #<zhigh>]
    G1 Z#<zhigh> F[#<f_tr>]
  o20 endif

  (protective descent, 1 in. A trip here means the rod is fouling something)
  (BEFORE any probing -- met during the +X probe instead, the same contact)
  (would be indistinguishable from a real touch.)
  G38.3 Z#<zref> F[#<f_ck>]
  o30 if [#5070 EQ 1]
    G90
    G1 Z#<zhigh> F[#<f_tr>]
    M65 P3
    (abort, GO TO C REF: contact on the way down - the rod is fouling something. Nothing was probed.)
  o30 endif

  (PRINT, GO TO C REF: side #<side>, X offset #3061, Y offset side x #3058, depth #3060 below top. Puck is UP - verify the tip is in the ballpark.)
o<cal_c_goto> endsub

M2 (end program)
